## Getting started

Node is the version in [`.node-version`](.node-version).

```sh
npm ci
{%- if 'e2e' in test_types %}
npx playwright install chromium
{%- endif %}
cp .env.example .env    # then set BASE_URL to the system under test
npm run smoke
```

| Command | What it runs |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run check` | Type check, lint, format check and the Dependabot ignore sentinel (`scripts/check-dependency-ignores.ts`) |
| `npm test` | The whole suite |
| `npm run smoke` | Only the tests tagged `@smoke` |

In CI, set `BASE_URL` as an Actions variable of the repository. The `audit` job fails on a known vulnerability in `package-lock.json` (exceptions and their policy: [`osv-scanner.toml`](osv-scanner.toml)), and each run keeps its HTML report as the `playwright-report` artifact.

A command run by a Claude Code tool gets the `dot` reporter (one character per test, failures in full); a terminal gets `list`.
